{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779059729,"nonce":"XLfpq1RBpN9FMZqtQry28rrAOCA=","message":"## Current remaining work after Phase 1-3 foundation merges\n\nThis roadmap issue already exists as the cross-repo coordination issue, so no new umbrella was created. This comment updates the remaining work after the recent completed foundation slices:\n\nCompleted foundation now available:\n- Phase 1 Feedbax provider/manifest MVP: `5429a23`, merged in `947fc24`. Feedbax can emit provider manifests, validate core specs, expose registries/capabilities over Python/CLI/HTTP, write durable manifests, store local artifacts, and rebuild a manifest index.\n- Phase 2 Mandible provider/artifact ingest slice: Mandible `e991df8`, merged in `ed14424`. Mandible can ingest native Feedbax provider/run/spec/report-style manifests into provider/artifact records and provider-lineage graph nodes/edges.\n- Phase 3 deterministic execution-contract slice: `c6b1b73`, merged in `ceb299c`. Feedbax now has `ExecutionSpec` / `ExecutionPlan` for local, SSH, RunPod, and Modal; local execution emits a manifest; RunPod and Modal have concrete inspectable plan/app generation surfaces but not live credentialed submission.\n- Related Mandible infrastructure: canonical ledger work from Mandible `097d2b7`, unified chat/app-shell foundations, and post-merge generated-dist cleanup have also landed, but they do not close the product-level graph/Studio phases below.\n\nWhat remains by phase:\n\n### Phase 1 residuals — Feedbax provider contract depth\nPrimary issues: `c6c6da0`, `f68cf66`.\n\nThe MVP substrate exists, but the broader provider contract remains open:\n- Provider-driven evaluation, analysis, and report execution that emit `EvaluationRunManifest`, `AnalysisRunManifest`, and `ReportManifest` as first-class outputs.\n- Better schema coverage for task/loss/objective/analysis/report specs and project-defined extension packages.\n- Project/package registration cleanup, especially moving project routing/config toward durable package metadata rather than ad hoc registration calls.\n- Migration/import of old run/eval/figure database records into manifests where possible, with uncertainty marked when old provenance is incomplete.\n- Artifact publication handoff: Feedbax should accept/store Mandible artifact IDs when Mandible is present while remaining standalone with local refs.\n- Provider entry points/actions such as open in Studio, inspect run/report, validate selected spec, and publish/import/export.\n\n### Phase 2 residuals — Mandible graph/provider/artifact product layer\nPrimary Mandible issues: `de2f8ac`, `2472c51`, plus graph/layout follow-ups such as `b45f19b`.\n\nThe backend ingest path exists, but the graph workspace and provider action model still need product-hardening:\n- Data-driven selected-node detail panes and hover previews for provider specs, runs, analyses, reports, artifacts, issues, sessions, and auth/work objects.\n- Better graph layout semantics: issue-centric auth relationships, deterministic umbrella/subgraph geometry, live-session overlays, hidden edge labels by default, and provider/provenance layouts that do not degenerate into unreadable stacks.\n- Provider action registry and reviewed provider actions: validate, open, preview, execute, import/export, publish, and artifact actions should appear based on provider capability + selected node compatibility + policy.\n- Artifact retention/storage UX and policy: local content-addressed storage exists conceptually, but retention, pinning, cleanup, external stores, and user-visible artifact inspection are not done.\n- Canonical issue/provider reference resolution: Feedbax provenance issue refs are currently provider-scoped where needed; they should resolve through central Mandible project/issue alias policy rather than Feedbax-only assumptions.\n- Clear distinction between exhaustive provenance graph and curated semantic graph edges.\n\n### Phase 3 residuals — live cloud/worker execution\nPrimary closed slice: `c6b1b73`; needs one or more new concrete children before live execution work.\n\nThe plan/schema layer is done; live execution is not:\n- Generic SSH worker runner: bootstrap, health, launch, monitor, log streaming, status, artifact sync, and manifest finalization against a real supplied host.\n- RunPod adapter: create/attach pod, poll SSH readiness from the correct fields, execute through the SSH worker contract, sync artifacts back, stop/cleanup pods, and classify allocation/SSH/env/JAX/training failures.\n- Modal adapter: submit generated app, map/spawn_map independent cells, stream/collect logs/status, commit/sync volume outputs, and emit/finalize manifests/artifact refs.\n- Environment provenance: package lock/env metadata, GPU/driver/JAX/platform metadata, dirty patch artifacts when local dev overrides are used.\n- Mandible integration later: reviewed/credentialed provider actions should call the Feedbax execution contract rather than implementing RunPod/Modal logic in Mandible UI code.\n\n### Phase 4 — Feedbax Studio vertical slice\nPrimary issues: `0c46f69`, `5378a5d`, with concrete children still to split before coding.\n\nThis is now the main remaining MVP product phase:\n- A saved Studio workspace/pipeline model with train/eval/analysis/report stages.\n- Stage-owned scenario/spec drafts rather than global hidden training/task/loss state.\n- Collection semantics: training collections, eval over selected model/run collections, analysis over selected eval/artifact collections, and report/product stubs.\n- Eval inheritance/override semantics from training scenarios.\n- Executions from Studio routed through the provider/execution contract and emitting manifests/artifact refs.\n- Studio remains standalone, with Mandible ingest as enrichment rather than dependency.\n\n### Phase 5 — Studio pipeline/scenario refactor\nPrimary issues: `0c46f69`, `5378a5d`, `93f79f2`.\n\nAfter the vertical slice works, migrate the existing app state into the intended architecture:\n- `trainingStore.trainingSpec/taskSpec` becomes stage/scenario-owned state.\n- Loss/task editing moves toward `ScenarioSpec`, `ObjectiveTermSpec`, typed selectors, and shared temporal selectors.\n- `runStore` becomes collection/selection state attached to stages.\n- Analysis pages become analysis-stage specs over selected input collections.\n- Autosave persists workspace/stages/scenarios/spec drafts and executed snapshots, not only graph and analysis pages.\n- Top pane becomes stage-aware structural/scenario authoring; bottom pane becomes pipeline/provenance workspace.\n\n### Phase 6 — richer UX and workflow integration\nPrimary issues include Feedbax `93f79f2`, Mandible `0516fc0`, Mandible `80f18c0`, and later child issues.\n\nThis should follow the core vertical path, not precede it:\n- Better Mandible graph filters, clustering, previews, inspectors, provider actions, and curated semantic edges.\n- Studio visual objective/task/biomechanics authoring and richer 2D/3D views.\n- Report authoring/product management.\n- Better remote execution provisioning UX.\n- Agent-assisted spec generation and reviewed extension registration.\n- Continued Mandible chat/app-shell/project-registry polish where it supports the broader research control-plane workflow.\n\nRecommended next implementation step: split a concrete Phase 4 Feedbax Studio vertical-slice child issue before coding. The highest-risk remaining boundary is visible Studio state vs durable specs/manifests; cloud execution now has a contract surface, but Studio still needs to stop relying on hidden frontend-only or global-store interpretation for executable semantics.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}